  "notes": "USAGE:\n{青|あお}ざめる is most often used with {顔|かお} (face) as the subject, or with the person as the subject (implying their face). The past participle {青|あお}ざめた is frequently used as a modifier: {青|あお}ざめた{顔|かお} (a pale face).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {顔|かお}が{青|あお}ざめる (one's face turns pale)\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}で{青|あお}ざめる (to turn pale with fear)\n- {青|あお}ざめた{顔|かお} (a pale/ashen face)\n- {青|あお}ざめた{表情|ひょうじょう} (a pale expression)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {青|あお}ざめる: to turn pale (face loses color; fear/shock)\n- {青白|あおじろ}い: pale, pallid (adjective describing complexion)\n- {血|ち}の{気|け}が{引|ひ}く: the blood drains from one's face (stronger expression)",
